<head>
<title>Mut Mee Guest House Nong Khai Thailand, Accommodation, Yoga, Restaurant, Reiki, Maekong River, Bookshop, Massage, Sculpture Park Salakaewkoo, Isan, Isarn, Esarn, NongKhai, Nong Kai, Mekong River, Mekong Riverbank Garden, Mat Mee, MutMee, Vientiane, Laos, Friendship Bridge, Thai Visa, Lao Visa, Thai Food, Astrology, Retirement Homes, Fireballs, North East Thailand, Northeast Thailand.</title>
<META name="Author" content="Julian Wright, Nong Khai, Thailand">
<META name="description" content="Guest House in Nong Khai, North East Thailand, set in a beautiful garden overlooking the Maekong River. Featuring a bookshop, yoga courses, massage, fitness training, reiki, astrology. Nong Khai town has a world class Sculpture Park (Salakeawkoo), the Serpents Fireballs (Bang Fii Pyanak), Rocket Festivals, and the 3500 year old Phu Prabat Historical Park.">
<META name="keywords" content="Guest House, Guest-House, Gest House, Nong Khai, Accommodation in Thailand, Thailand, North-East Thailand, North East Thailand, Maekong River, Mekong River, Maekong, Mekong, Backpacking, Sculpture Park, Salakeawkoo, Phu Prabat Historical Park, Biking, bicycling, cycling, Isarn, Esarn, Esan, Isan, Laos, Lao, Vientiane, Vang Vieng, yoga, astrology, fitness, reiki, ayurvedic, massage, Bang Fai Pyanak, Bang Fii Payanak, Fireballs, Visa to Laos, Lao Visa, Laos Visa, Friendship Bridge, Volunteer Work, Teaching in Thailand, tours, touring, Thai Food, Thai Cooking, Anou Savari, Song Kran, marathon, King’s Birthday marathon, Rocket Festivals, Loy Kratong, Christmas in Thailand, New Year in Thailand, Nang Usa, Wat Phu Tok, Wat Hin Mak Peng, Wat Hin Maak Peng, Ban Chiang, Bridge to Laos, River Beach, Wet Lands, Sunset Boat, Udorn, Udon, Udon Thani, Sang Khom, Naga, Naga Lands, Nagalands, Maekong Fireballs, Mekong Fireballs">
<META name="content-language" content="en-us">
<META name="Distribution" content="Global">
